 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Calm ambient only. Dawn for the opening (the Book sent down), rays of light for the warning and the good tidings (Paradise is never drawn: the reward gloss has no arrow), geometric pattern for the refutation of the claim of a son. No light effect is placed on the Name of Allah itself. v2: the crowd plate (4:2) now leaves before the Name in 4:5; a sideways pan replaces the push-in that ran into the Name. No clouds part on 1:4: they gathered around the geometric plate of the Name (1:2) and their rays converged on it; a sideways pan instead. v2b: no sparkle on 1:7 (it flashed on the sun the gloss about the Prophet pointed at): a pan instead."
 },
